      "notes": "## Rotation\n1. **Hall of Mirrors (1):** Clones draw aggro and split enemy fire.\n2. **Xata's Whisper (2, Helminth, replaces Sleight of Hand):** Adds Void damage to your weapons.\n3. **Hold Eclipse (3):** Weapon damage buff. If things get rough, tap it for damage reduction instead.\n4. Charge-throw **[[Glaive Prime]]** into the group, detonate it mid-air, charge again right away.\n5. Recast buffs before they run out. Energy comes from health orbs via [[Equilibrium]].\nPrism (4) is optional in this build.\n\n## Why it works\n- **[[Primed Flow]] + Violet Archon Shards:** Above 500 max energy, the shards' melee crit damage doubles. Without Primed Flow you lose half of the shard bonus.\n- **[[Melee Duplicate]]:** Yellow crits hit a second time. Crit chance above 100% barely pays off here, because orange crits aren't duplicated.\n- **[[Arcane Fury]]:** Crits trigger the melee damage buff. With over 80% crit chance, it's up almost permanently.\n- **[[Galvanized Reflex]] + [[Melee Elementalist]]:** Heavy attacks cost less combo and kills grant Initial Combo. You charge faster and deal more status damage.\n- **[[Primed Fever Strike]]:** Toxin bypasses shields, and its procs keep [[Growing Power]] active.\n- **[[Blind Rage]] / [[Narrow Minded]]:** Efficiency and range are sacrificed on purpose. The build barely needs range, and [[Equilibrium]] covers the energy cost.\n\n## Survival\n- Mirage only has around 900 effective health, so keep moving.\n- [[Rolling Guard]]: Rolling makes you briefly invulnerable and removes status effects.\n- Thanks to [[Equilibrium]], energy orbs heal you as well.\n- In an emergency, tap Eclipse for damage reduction.\n\n## Variants\n- **No Violet shards:** Use Crimson shards with melee crit damage. This frees up the [[Primed Flow]] slot.\n- **No Primed Flow:** Arcane Battery also raises max energy and counts toward the shards, but it costs an arcane slot.\n- **Group play:** Swap in Total Eclipse, e.g. for [[Natural Talent]] (check capacity). Allies within 15 m and your clones get the Eclipse buff.\n- **Tip:** You can swap tap/hold for abilities in the settings, so the damage buff sits on tap.",
